IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pra71-rules`

§ `Tests`

GIVEN k IS A `Pension class 1971`, amt IS A NUMBER, hus IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Increase position 1971`
`for` k `on` amt `husband` hus MEANS `the increase position for` (`Pensioner 1971` OF k, amt, hus, Date 14 10 1971)

#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 48.16 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 13.98
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 63.79 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 16.78
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 50 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`for` `an annual pensioner under s 4` `on` 2729.17 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 729.16
#ASSERT (`for` `an annual pensioner under s 5` `on` 3812.86 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 875
#ASSERT (`for` `an office-holder under s 6` `on` 23.33 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 11.36
#ASSERT (`for` `an office-holder or widow under s 7` `on` 1260 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 220.5
#ASSERT (`for` `a widow under s 3(2)` `on` 0 `husband` 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 62.14
#ASSERT (`for` `a widow under s 4(2)` `on` 0 `husband` 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 3458.33
#ASSERT (`for` `a widow under s 5(2)` `on` 0 `husband` 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 3645.83
-- s 6(2): husband's $28 pension rose by $13.63: five-sixths.
#ASSERT (`for` `a widow under s 6(2)` `on` 10 `husband` 28)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST (5/6 TIMES 13.63)
#ASSERT (`for` `a former Prime Minister's widow under s 8` `on` 1000 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 48.16 `husband` 0)'s `from` EQUALS JUST (Date 14 10 1971)
#ASSERT (`for` `none of these` `on` 48.16 `husband` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS NOTHING
